+- Format before committing. CI runs the hooks in [.pre-commit-config.yaml](.pre-commit-config.yaml) via [prek](https://prek.j178.dev), whose `julia-formatter` hook uses the version-pinned [.dev/format](.dev/format) environment (currently JuliaFormatter `=2.10.1`) against this repo's `.JuliaFormatter.toml` (margin 80). Install the hooks once with `uv tool install prek && prek install`, or match CI by hand with either `prek run --all-files` or the pinned environment directly: `julia --startup-file=no --project=.dev/format -e 'using Pkg; Pkg.instantiate(io=devnull); using JuliaFormatter; format(ARGS)' .`. Avoid `format(".")` from your base environment -- `Pkg.add("JuliaFormatter")` may install a different version, which produces a different diff.
 - Prefer `Pkg.test()` over manually `include`ing `test/runtests.jl`: test-only deps (e.g. `JET`) are loaded through the package test path.
 - For a local docs build, `Pkg.develop(path = pwd())` in the `docs` environment first (the committed `docs/Manifest.toml` can be stale); restore it with `git checkout docs/Manifest.toml` before committing, never mid-build.
 - Match existing style: explicit names, narrow imports, comments that explain why. Follow the CliMA documentation policy (explicit `# Fields` sections in struct docstrings, not `DocStringExtensions.FIELDS`).
diff --git a/RRTMGP.jl/NEWS.md b/RRTMGP.jl-mod/NEWS.md
index 75e12f3..f51e5c5 100644
--- a/RRTMGP.jl/NEWS.md
+++ b/RRTMGP.jl-mod/NEWS.md
@@ -4,6 +4,25 @@ RRTMGP.jl Release Notes
 main
 ----
 
+- [#637](https://github.com/CliMA/RRTMGP.jl/pull/637) `TwoStreamLWRTE` and
+  `TwoStreamSWRTE` solve a column's g-point loop in `ngpt_groups` independent
+  pieces covered by one grid, in place of the serial loop each thread ran over
+  its own column, and compute each round's gas and aerosol optics in a kernel
+  of its own before sweeping them. **Default results change at roundoff.** The
+  group count is chosen per grid by `default_ngpt_groups` and is above one on a
+  GPU wherever the column count leaves the device underfilled, which reorders
+  the g-point sum; floating-point addition is not associative, so grouped
+  fluxes differ from a serial solve by about 1e-6 relative in the
+  configurations tested, and the clear-sky half of a both-skies solve no longer
+  equals a standalone clear-sky solve exactly. The cloud-cover tally is a count
+  of g-points and stays exact. Pass `ngpt_groups = 1` to any two-stream
+  constructor where bit-for-bit agreement with the serial order is required;
+  that is also what a CPU gets, whose driver ignores the grouped workspaces.
+  Grouping costs device memory: every widened workspace is linear in the group
+  count, the accumulators being `ncol * ngpt_groups * nlev` by two flux planes
+  in the longwave and three in the shortwave, so a run tight on memory should
+  pass a smaller `ngpt_groups` rather than take the default.
+
 v1.1.0
 ------
 
